WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.914
- [Male] I think Laz is
crazy, but in a very good way.

00:00:04.914 --> 00:00:07.150
I think he's very smart, I
think he knows what he's doing.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.948
- [Male 2] People think
he's a sadist, or whatever.

00:00:09.948 --> 00:00:11.239
- [Female] He's like my trail soulmate.

00:00:11.239 --> 00:00:12.494
- [Male 2] Flare for the dramatic, I think.

00:00:12.494 --> 00:00:13.744
- [Female] Bit of a sassy man.

00:00:13.744 --> 00:00:15.224
(Laz laughs)

00:00:15.224 --> 00:00:16.935
- [Narrator] Laz Cantrell,

00:00:16.935 --> 00:00:20.438
a true backwoods rebel
of Tennessee, created one

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:23.370
of the world's most grueling footraces.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.408
One that is so challenging, it leads many

00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:28.167
to assume it must be an act of sadism.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.803
(Laz laughs)

00:00:30.803 --> 00:00:32.756
Are you a sadist?

00:00:32.756 --> 00:00:33.943
- No, no.

00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:36.468
I think people are obsessed with comfort

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:38.933
to the point that they forget if you don't

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:40.720
have any discomfort in your life,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.637
how do you know when you feel good?

00:00:46.707 --> 00:00:49.536
The Barkley Marathons is a 100-mile race

00:00:49.536 --> 00:00:51.920
comprised of five 20-mile loops, 

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.837
which you have 60 hours to complete.

00:00:55.998 --> 00:00:58.510
And so, there's some
pretty rugged terrain.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.677
It's got a massive amount
of climb, about 66,000 feet.

00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:07.081
You have just your map and compass.

00:01:07.081 --> 00:01:11.428
It's cold, it's wet, it’s
miserable, you're alone.

00:01:11.428 --> 00:01:13.124
The fact that they’ll probably

00:01:13.124 --> 00:01:17.538
almost certainly fail
makes it more appealing.

00:01:17.538 --> 00:01:21.288
This started in '85 and, uh,
we have 14 finishers.

00:01:24.614 --> 00:01:26.447
Are y'all about ready?

00:01:27.366 --> 00:01:30.169
- [Female] You start the
race with a cigarette light,

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:33.580
which feels very untraditional
for most race starts.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.472
- [Laz] Yeah, we always
use a Camel because

00:01:35.472 --> 00:01:38.454
that's about the best cigarette, I think.

00:01:38.454 --> 00:01:41.599
- [Male] Yay team, go for it.

00:01:41.599 --> 00:01:44.182
(crowd cheers)

00:01:45.715 --> 00:01:46.627
- [Narrator] The course is located

00:01:46.627 --> 00:01:48.832
in Frozen Head State Park,

00:01:48.832 --> 00:01:52.157
home to the Brushy Mountain
State Penitentiary.

00:01:52.157 --> 00:01:55.012
A location not chosen by chance.

00:01:55.012 --> 00:01:58.245
(ominous music)

00:01:58.245 --> 00:02:00.324
In 1977, James Earl Ray,

00:02:00.324 --> 00:02:03.172
the man who killed Martin Luther King Jr.,

00:02:03.172 --> 00:02:07.296
made headlines again when
he escaped the prison.

00:02:07.296 --> 00:02:09.114
In the 54 hours he was free,

00:02:09.114 --> 00:02:13.009
he only made it eight miles from his cell.

00:02:13.009 --> 00:02:15.676
Because this terrain is no joke.

00:02:16.674 --> 00:02:18.241
- It donned on us; I thought man, you could put together

00:02:18.241 --> 00:02:22.408
a racecourse that would really
challenge people's soul.

00:02:23.365 --> 00:02:25.919
I think every runner
would like to do better

00:02:25.919 --> 00:02:28.918
than James Earl Ray, and get
further than eight miles.

00:02:28.918 --> 00:02:33.085
Although, some of them don't (laughs).

00:02:34.949 --> 00:02:38.257
Everybody gets a bid number for each loop.

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.440
There's paperback books, which are kind

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.741
of strategically placed so that to get

00:02:42.741 --> 00:02:46.366
them all you have to follow the course.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:51.178
And you pull out the page number
that matches your bid.

00:02:51.178 --> 00:02:52.914
You have to turn in your pages

00:02:52.914 --> 00:02:55.497
to show you've done the course.

00:02:57.324 --> 00:02:59.256
- He has a brilliant sense of humor.

00:02:59.256 --> 00:03:03.456
He's parodying the sport
of ultra-marathon running.

00:03:03.456 --> 00:03:07.411
Those of us who run ultras,
we have a certain egoism

00:03:07.411 --> 00:03:09.271
that we think we're pretty good

00:03:09.271 --> 00:03:10.567
because of what we can do.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:14.313
And, so, he set out to
puncture that balloon.

00:03:14.313 --> 00:03:18.030
Laz keeps making it
harder because he's trying

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.697
to put it at the limit
of human possibility.

00:03:24.121 --> 00:03:26.538
(bugle Taps)

00:03:31.718 --> 00:03:33.875
- After they've decided
that they've had enough

00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:36.931
and quit, we play Taps on the bugle.

00:03:36.931 --> 00:03:39.283
Both because Taps is what you play

00:03:39.283 --> 00:03:42.077
for someone who's died in action,

00:03:42.077 --> 00:03:45.077
and because they will be tapped-out.

00:03:49.448 --> 00:03:50.891
- I think, genuinely in his heart,

00:03:50.891 --> 00:03:53.474
he wants to see people succeed.

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:56.664
When people actually finish five loops,

00:03:56.664 --> 00:03:57.766
and you see him at the end,

00:03:57.766 --> 00:03:59.383
he's so excited.

00:03:59.383 --> 00:04:01.821
(crowd cheers)

00:04:01.821 --> 00:04:04.643
- When you have one or
more of them comes in,

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:06.723
it's an inspiring thing.

00:04:06.723 --> 00:04:11.545
It's hard to believe a
human can accomplish that.

00:04:11.545 --> 00:04:14.034
It's good that some years no one finishes

00:04:14.034 --> 00:04:17.701
'cause The Barkley
should win sometimes, too.

